WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Articulate 360 is best understood as an eLearning authoring ecosystem rather than a single

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.865
magic button for training.

00:00:06.865 --> 00:00:11.020
It brings together tools for building courses, creating interactions, managing review,

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.500
using media assets, and publishing learning content for online delivery.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.660
In a practical training team, that means one environment may support slide-based courses,

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.555
responsive lessons, assessments, stakeholder review, and LMS-ready output.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.905
It helps to separate the parts of the ecosystem.

00:00:24.905 --> 00:00:27.580
Authoring tools are where the course is designed and built.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.460
Review tools support comments, approvals, and revisions.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.820
Media assets provide starting points for visuals, icons, templates,

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.395
and character-style elements.

00:00:35.395 --> 00:00:37.960
Publishing formats control how the course is delivered,

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:41.420
while the learning platform or LMS handles launch, tracking, reporting,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.510
and learner access.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:46.330
Common use cases include compliance training, technical training, onboarding,

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:50.680
microlearning, software training, product education, and scenario-based decision practice.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.050
These courses may look very different from one another.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.790
A short policy refresher might need a clean responsive structure and a simple quiz.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.860
A software workflow course might need demonstrations and practice.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.880
A leadership scenario might need branching decisions and feedback.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.040
The tool does not replace instructional design.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.000
Strong courses begin with a reason for learning, a learner audience, a performance gap,

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.185
and a clear outcome.

00:01:10.185 --> 00:01:13.235
Features matter, but features without purpose can create clutter.

00:01:13.235 --> 00:01:16.720
The best Articulate 360 projects use the tool to support learning,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.480
not to show off every interaction or animation available.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:23.880
A useful way to frame Articulate 360 work is to treat each project as a learning product

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:24.810
with a lifecycle.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.440
It begins with a need, moves through design and development,

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.600
passes through review and testing, and eventually needs updates.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.010
Thinking in lifecycle terms keeps the team from focusing only on the initial build and

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.060
forgetting maintainability,

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:37.920
tracking, and learner support.
